<title>USA: United Dominion settles EPA complaint.</title>
<headline>United Dominion settles EPA complaint.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) Region 5 said Tuesday it settled a civil complaint filed against United Dominion Industries Ltd.</p>
<p>The company was cited for failing to report data on toxic chemicals used at its Van Wert, Ohio, plant in a timely manner, the EPA said.</p>
<p>United Dominion will pay a $23,658 fine and complete an environmental project that will cost at least $278,377, the EPA said. The project includes using water-based paints at the facility instead of solvent-based paints.</p>
<p>The company makes prefabricated building components.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
